  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A model or scene loaded by name is read again into what the program holds as its file is saved, with the guide to editing while a program runs.\nA live program reads a texture again as its file is saved and draws it under the same handle, at its new size where it has one.\nA live program compiles a shader again as its file is saved and draws with it under the same handle, keeping the old one where the save does not compile.\nThe measure against raylib finds the SDL version in the library's projects, and the first wait after a game opens gives a cold compile ten minutes.\nA program is live where it runs from its own project's build folder or says so, watching the files the flat API loads by name and loading each again once quiet, which e3d's live lists.\nTwo comments say what the code does, the glow lights' share and the games the pack run plays on Windows and macOS.\nComments say the reason alone, their readings before and after, their measured costs and their accounts of trials left to the documents and the review.",
